{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/496676-argos-black-wings","id":496676,"title":"Argos black wings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-29T13:16:00-07:00","id":496676,"title":"Argos black wings","content":"Hi<br /> <br /> I'm trying to set a game of Wraith the oblivion. I knew the game for several years and now I'm re-reading it again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I swear I remember that the power Phantom Wings of Argos arcanos gave the Wraith well... black phantom wings. But no matter how many times I read it, the power description doesn't say it explicitly.<br /> <br /> Now, I just read in one of Eriks stories that he manifested his wings while using the mentioned arcanos... so, my question is... does the black wings feature for the power exists? Or am I just extrapolating things? Am I crazy?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5712-daraexus","name":"Daraexus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5712_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:20:29-07:00","id":496688,"title":"","content":"The wings can look however the hell you want.<br /> <br /> Black-feathered angel wings? Sure. Butterfly wings made of broken stained glass? Alright. Tattered strips of stained silk? Nothing stopping you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T13:38:12-07:00","id":496710,"title":"","content":"But my question is... where is this on the Wraith books? I cannot recall where this was stated...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5712-daraexus","name":"Daraexus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5712_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T14:41:16-07:00","id":496793,"title":"","content":"Argos level 2 - Phantom Wings. One literally grows wings to glide and fly through the Tempest. The write up in the core book literally says &quot;the Harbinger can grow wings.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> Edit: Holy shit, I just looked it up, and nowhere in the book does it say the character gets actual wings - it's just implied through the name and artwork. I'm curious now - can we find the explicit statement in the books that says a character gets wings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 04-29-2015, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:15:59-07:00","id":497028,"title":"","content":"You are quite right! However, the text for the Wraith20 clearly says that the powers bestows wings. But indeed neither first or second edition did explicitly say so. We can guess that actual wings has always been the design for the power, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T05:25:54-07:00","id":497340,"title":"","content":"That's what I thought. I was sure to have read the wings thing somewhere, but besides the little narrations on the books... I found nothing literal.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Wraith20 is a thing from now, but how did we assume that Phantom Wings grow wings? The Mnemoi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5712-daraexus","name":"Daraexus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5712_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:46:01-07:00","id":497502,"title":"","content":"The picture next to the power has a Harbinger with big wings. Then the comic strip gameplay example later in the book has a character sprout wings too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T11:15:15-07:00","id":497643,"title":"","content":"We've never had them grow wings. They float. Ghosts float a lot in the appropriate stories. <br /> <br /> There really isn't another way for them to do that in the rules. So... floating, flying ghosties without the affectation of wings. (Well, there are a lot of very situation specific workarounds, but not just &quot;you're not bound by gravity.&quot;) You want to grow wings? Get Moliate. You want to be able to float ('cause it's really not much in the way of flying)? Get Argos. You want to flap your Moliated wings while you use Argos to float? Sure. Pretty.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:14:52-07:00","id":502549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/496676-argos-black-wings?p=497502#post497502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then the comic strip gameplay example later in the book has a character sprout wings too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you even see them start to grow out of her back as they make their big escape.<br /> <br /> Given how one of the characters in the story seems to have a... semi-detachable head*... I think we can safely assume wraiths are pretty malleable in appearance. Wings or no wings, or crazy fancy wings (Stained glass buttefly wings... cool!) is all gravy.<br /> <br /> *I am pretty sure that tripod thing with strings he wears is how he keeps his head upright most of the time... the spectre just took the opportunity to tug it loose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:52:08-07:00","id":502561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given how one of the characters in the story seems to have a... semi-detachable head*... I think we can safely assume wraiths are pretty malleable in appearance. </div> </div> </div>And considering that Guildbook: Masquers has a headless flaw in it, the head is still attached to you by a thin string of plasm, I would say you are correct. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:48:08-07:00","id":505886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/496676-argos-black-wings?p=502561#post502561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And considering that Guildbook: Masquers has a headless flaw in it...</div> </div> </div> </div>I just gotta say, as one who never read any of the supplements for Guilds, I really love that such a Flaw exists... I cannot say exactly WHY I love it, but then again, I cannot say exactly why I love <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> as fervently as I do. I mean, it's a love on a level that words fail to describe, you know?<br /> <br /> Heck, where am I? I'm SURE you know! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}